2. Help teams prioritise the review queue
An EHS team may have many open observations, but they do not all require the same response.

Useful context includes the potential consequence, the condition of relevant controls, repeated findings, affected activities and how long an action has remained unresolved.

AI can help organise this information and surface records for attention. Any prioritisation method should remain understandable to the people using it.

A frequently reported minor concern must not automatically outrank a rare concern with potentially severe consequences. Frequency is one input, not a complete measure of risk.

