3. Bring previous learning into work preparation
Before a maintenance activity starts, supervisors need more than the current permit form. Relevant past findings may help them ask better questions about the planned work.

For example:

Has a similar task generated repeated observations?

Are related corrective actions still outstanding?

Have working conditions changed since the assessment?

Are nearby activities creating additional coordination needs?

A connected implementation can make these records easier to find during preparation.

