Frequently asked questions
How does AI support power plant safety?
AI can help analyse incident reports, near misses and inspection findings, identify recurring themes and prioritise records for human review. Its usefulness depends on data quality, configuration and follow-through.

Can AI predict every power plant incident?
No. Unrecorded conditions, changing work and incomplete information limit prediction. AI supports risk management; it does not guarantee incident prevention.

What data is needed to get started?
A focused implementation can begin with well-structured observations, inspection findings and corrective-action records. Additional data sources should be introduced when they serve a defined purpose and can be integrated reliably.

Does a low AI risk score mean work is safe?
No. A score reflects a model and its available inputs. Required assessments, physical controls, checks and authorisations still apply.

Make reporting the start of action
Power plant teams already hold valuable knowledge in their observations, inspections and investigations.

AI can help them connect that knowledge and identify where to look more closely. The improvement happens when those insights lead to accountable decisions and verified action.

